globalThis.ragSearchTexts=globalThis.ragSearchTexts||{};globalThis.ragSearchTexts["448"]={"510":"Intro — mlcourse.ai\nИз публикации: Онлайн-книга mlcourse.ai\nIntro — mlcourse.ai\n\nРазделы страницы: Intro#; How to navigate this website and pass the course#; Bonus assignments#; About the course#\n\nIntro\nContents\nIntro#\nHow to navigate this website and pass the course#\nBonus assignments#\nAbout the course#\n\nIntro#\nmlcourse.ai – Open Machine Learning Course\nmlcourse.ai is an open Machine Learning course by OpenDataScience, led by Yury Kashnitsky (yorko), now Staff GenAI Forward Deployed Engineer at Google Cloud. Having both a Ph.D. degree in applied math and a Kaggle Competitions Master tier, Yury aimed at designing an ML course with a perfect balance between theory and practice. Thus, the course meets you with math formulae in lectures, and a lot of practice in a form of assignments and Kaggle Inclass competitions. The course covers the foundations of machine learning, though neural networks and GenAI are out of scope. Currently, the course is in a self-paced mode. Here we guide you through the self-paced mlcourse.ai.\nIn the following short video we discuss how to best approach the course material:\nHow to navigate this website and pass the course#\nHere you see a Jupyter book – an executable book containing MarkDown, code, images, graphs, etc. (we describe Jupyter books in more detail later). You can jump forward and backward with left and right arrows. Any page can be downloaded as .md (MarkDown) or PDF – use the Download button in the upper-right corner. For every page, you can see its source on GitHub, and you can also open an issue or suggest an edit – use the GitHub button in the upper-right corner.\nOK, let’s go! First, check prerequisites, then you see 10 topics – from exploratory data analysis with Pandas to gradient boosting. For each topic, there’s an introductory part (here’s an example for Topic 1) that lists articles","511":"Intro — mlcourse.ai\nИз публикации: Онлайн-книга mlcourse.ai\nrerequisites, then you see 10 topics – from exploratory data analysis with Pandas to gradient boosting. For each topic, there’s an introductory part (here’s an example for Topic 1) that lists articles to read, lectures to watch and assignments to crack.\nBonus assignments#\nAdditionally, you can purchase a Bonus Assignments pack with the best non-demo versions of mlcourse.ai assignments. Select the “Bonus Assignments” tier on Patreon or a similar tier on Boosty (rus).\nDetails of the deal\nmlcourse.ai is still in self-paced mode but we offer you Bonus Assignments with solutions for a contribution of $17/month. The idea is that you pay for ~1-5 months while studying the course materials, but a single contribution is still fine and opens your access to the bonus pack.\nNote: the first payment is charged at the moment of joining the Tier Patreon, and the next payment is charged on the 1st day of the next month, thus it’s better to purchase the pack in the 1st half of the month.\nmlcourse.ai is never supposed to go fully monetized (it’s created in the wonderful open ODS.ai community and will remain open and free) but it’d help to cover some operational costs, and Yury also put in quite some effort into assembling all the best assignments into one pack. Please note that unlike the rest of the course content, Bonus Assignments are copyrighted. Informally, Yury’s fine if you share the pack with 2-3 friends but public sharing of the Bonus Assignments pack is prohibited.\nThe bonus pack contains 10 assignments, in some of them you are challenged to beat a baseline in a Kaggle competition under thorough guidance (“Alice” and “Medium”) or implement an algorithm from scratch – efficient stochastic gradient descent classifier and gradient boosting.\nAbout the course#\nIf you scroll down","512":"Intro — mlcourse.ai\nИз публикации: Онлайн-книга mlcourse.ai\nion under thorough guidance (“Alice” and “Medium”) or implement an algorithm from scratch – efficient stochastic gradient descent classifier and gradient boosting.\nAbout the course#\nIf you scroll down here on the left, you see the “About the course” section with additional materials and information:\nOne of the assignments in the past mlcourse.ai sessions was to write a tutorial on almost any ML/DS-related topic. The result is seen on the Tutorials page;\nOne of the motivating features of the past mlcourse.ai sessions was the leaderboard. Top 100 participants of each session are listed on the Rating page;\nThe Resources page lists other resources constituting the course, e.g. YouTube playlists or Medium/Habr.com articles written in the past;\nAuthors and some of the mlcourse.ai contributors (there were too many to list all of them) are listed on the Contributors page. Acknowledgements are there as well.\n\nPython\nMath\nSoftware \u0026 DevOps\nTopic 1 Intro\nExploratory data analysis with Pandas\nVideolecture 1\nDemo Assignment 1 Task\nDemo Assignment 1 Solution\nBonus Assignment 1\nTopic 2 Intro\nVisual Data Analysis\nSeaborn, Matplotlib, Plotly\nVideolecture 2\nDemo Assignment 2 Task\nDemo Assignment 2 Solution\nBonus Assignment 2\nTopic 3 Intro\nClassification, Decision Trees \u0026 k Nearest Neighbors\nVideolecture 3\nDemo Assignment 3 Task\nDemo Assignment 3 Solution\nBonus Assignment 3\nTopic 4 Intro\nOrdinary Least Squares\nLinear classification\nAn illustrative example of logistic regression regularization\nWhen logistic regression is good and when it is not\nValidation and learning curves\nVideolecture 4\nDemo Assignment 4 Task\nDemo Assignment 4 Solution\nBonus Assignment 4\nTopic 5 Intro\nBagging\nRandom Forest\nFeature importance\nVideolecture 5\nDemo Assignment 5\nDemo Assignment 5 Solution\nBonus Assignment 5","513":"Intro — mlcourse.ai\nИз публикации: Онлайн-книга mlcourse.ai\nmo Assignment 4 Task\nDemo Assignment 4 Solution\nBonus Assignment 4\nTopic 5 Intro\nBagging\nRandom Forest\nFeature importance\nVideolecture 5\nDemo Assignment 5\nDemo Assignment 5 Solution\nBonus Assignment 5\nTopic 6 Intro\nFeature engineering \u0026 feature selection\nDemo Assignment 6 Task\nBonus Assignment 6\nTopic 7 Intro\nUnsupervised learning\nVideolecture 7\nDemo Assignment 7\nDemo Assignment 7 Solution\nBonus Assignment 7\nTopic 8 Intro\nVowpal Wabbit: Learning with Gigabytes of Data\nVideolecture 8\nDemo Assignment 8\nDemo Assignment 8 Solution\nBonus Assignment 8\nTopic 9 Intro\nTopic 9. Part 1. Time series analysis in Python\nPredicting the future with Facebook Prophet\nVideolecture 9\nDemo Assignment 9\nDemo Assignment 9 Solution\nBonus Assignment 9\nTopic 10 Intro\nGradient boosting\nVideolecture 10\nDemo Assignment 10\nBonus Assignment 10\nTutorials\nRating\nResources\nContributors\nRepository\nSuggest edit\nOpen issue\n.md\nmlcourse.ai\nmlcourse.ai\nYury Kashnitsky (yorko)\nmlcourse.ai\nshort video\nJupyter book\nlater\nprerequisites\nhere’s an example\nmlcourse.ai\n“Bonus Assignments” tier\nsimilar tier\nmlcourse.ai\nmlcourse.ai\nODS.ai\n“Alice”\n“Medium”\nclassifier\ngradient boosting\nmlcourse.ai\nTutorials\nmlcourse.ai\nRating\nResources\nmlcourse.ai\nContributors\nnext\n        Prerequisites","1887":"Онлайн-книга mlcourse.ai\nhttps://mlcourse.ai/book/index.html\n\nКраткое описание:\nОнлайн-книга mlcourse.ai по машинному обучению с теорией, практическими заданиями и организацией самостоятельного курса."};
